=== first BAD commit ===
c55a2714 10-03 12:37 perf: block the pre-flight scan on the ingest eventfd instead of spin-sleeping (W-PREFLIGHT)
The pre-flight scan counts input lines to size the geometric ramp's
initial batch. When pread returns 0 with ingest not yet complete it
means 'wait for more', and it did that with usleep(100) -- about 10k
wakeups in 5 s on a slow producer, where bash slept 78 times.

ring_copy_main already signals evfd_ingest_data after every chunk
(forkrun_ring.c:8279) so that wait can block; the pre-flight just
never used it. Two changes:

1. The wait branch now polls evfd_ingest_data / evfd_ingest_eof for a
   BOUNDED 50 ms, then drains. The bound matters: one of the three
   exit conditions (first worker spawns) is detected by re-reading
   active_waiters at the top of the loop, so an unbounded poll would
   stop us noticing it. The drain matters because an eventfd left
   readable makes the next poll return at once, rebuilding the spin one
   level up.

2. fr_py_ingest_data_post: the Python spill was os.read/os.pwrite and
   never signalled that eventfd, which is WHY the pre-flight had to
   sleep. It now pokes it per chunk, exactly where ring_copy_main does.
